# sdl2-0001: port Northfear's SDL vitagl video backend (branch vitagl at
# f99bb638f7eb, based on SDL 2.24.0) onto our SDL 2.32.8 pin. Deviations from
# the fork: vglInitExtended(0,960,544,12MiB,msaa-from-attribute) becomes
# vglInitWithCustomSizes(0,960,544, ram, cdram, phycont, cdlg,
# SCE_GXM_MULTISAMPLE_NONE), whose return value is a resolution-fallback flag;
# the four pool sizes come from the hints/env vars below (SDL_strtoul base 0,
# 0 disables a pool, defaults are conservative so vitaGL never claims memory
# newlib's 128 MiB, audio, SDL or kernel memblocks need):
#   SDL_VITA_VGL_RAM_POOL     default 96 MiB
#   SDL_VITA_VGL_CDRAM_POOL   default 64 MiB
#   SDL_VITA_VGL_PHYCONT_POOL default 16 MiB
#   SDL_VITA_VGL_CDLG_POOL    default 0x8C6000 (vitaGL's cdialog max)
# Unlike the fork, the GLES1 renderer stays off (SDL_VIDEO_OPENGL_ES/
# RENDER_OGL_ES): its *OES entry points have no vitaGL counterpart and no
# GLESv1 stubs exist outside the PVR tree; the ES2 renderer covers our
# consumers. The 2.24.0 screen-keyboard IME unification is expressed as extra
# SDL_VIDEO_VITA_VGL guards on 2.32.8's existing PVR paths (PVR behavior is
# untouched); EXTRA_LIBS carry this vitaGL pin's full closure (vitashark,
# mathneon, SceShaccCgExt, taihen_stub, SceShaccCg/SceKernelDmacMgr/SceIme
# stubs).
